 Iterable interface:
 Iterable interface is the root interface which makes an object eligible for iteration using enhanced for loop.
 
  
  collections implement iterable interface : 
  for example : 
  Arraylist -> List -> Collection -> Iterable
  
  -most important methods of iterable is iterator()
  Iteration<T> iterator()
  -it provide iterator onject which can move through elements one by one.
  
  concurrentModificationException
  =========================================================================
  concurrent modification exception occurs when a collection is modified unexpectedly while it is being iteration.

Structural modification: Adding or removing elements elements in such a way that is changes the structure of the collection.

concurrent does not mean mulitple threads,this exception occur even with a single  thread.

Reason for Exception when enhanced for loop is used : 
===================================================================
ArrayList internally uses Iterator.
-In the enhanced for loop the Iterator traverse/iterators the list.
-countriesList.remove() in example,modifies the list directly.
-Iterator detects unexpected modification in the structure.
-so, the concurrent modification exception is thrown.
-The problem is occured because the collection is modified directly while iterator is traversing the collection.

eg: countriesList.remove(country); //here remove is the method of arrayList. 

When Iterator is explicitly used : 
==================================================================
iterator.remove() is a method which is specifically designed to safely remove the current element during iterator.
eg : iterator.remove();

failfast:
========
ArrayList iterator is know as failfast iterator.
A Fail fast means when ever an iterator detects unexpected structural modification to the collection during iteration,the iterator quickly throws ConcurrentModificationException.
