 1==>List Interface : 
 ------------------------
 List extends collection interface.
 List represents the ordered collection of elements.
 List allows duplicates.
 List supports index-based operations.

Important methods of list : 
	-get(index)
	-set(index,element)
	-add(index,element)
	-remove(index)
	-indexOf(element)
	
Implementataion classes of list : 
	-ArrayList,LinkedList,vector->stack.
1.ArrayList :
	-ArrayList implements the List Interface.
	-It internally uses resizeable array.
	-It maintains insertion order.
	-It allows dupicates.
	-It has fast random access using index.
	(It internally implements Random access interface)
	-Time complexity is o(1)
	-Insertion and removal in the middle may require shifting of the elements 
	-ArrayList is not sychronized.
	-It is best suited for the search operations.
	 
2.LinkedList :
	-LinkedList implements List interface.
	-It internally works different from ArrayList.
	-It allows null
	-It maintains insertion order.
	-It allows nodes rather than a resizable array.
	-It also implements Deque interface.
	

 
 